A||||9||Adrift||T-tops from other cars that fit a fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||07-21-2001||12:04 PM||||Has anyone tried to adapt T-tops from another car to fit a fiero? I know it would take some work to find the proper sized roof, but it might be possible to find a somewhat close fit?<BR>Ari<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tom88gt||07-21-2001||01:09 PM||||I asked that question a while back and didn't get any help.  My guess is that it has not done, hence the lack of input.  I had assumed that a Firebird/Camaro top would work but found a nive t-top formula before I could really look into it.  Your best bet is going to be to just but a t-top fiero.  They can be found on occasion.  Second option is to find a junkyard fiero t-top and cut the top off and put it on yours(involed but doable).||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||07-21-2001||01:55 PM||||I visited the original manufacturer of the GM T-tops (formerly cars & concepts) and my dad had the last "factory t-top" installed on his '88 GT.  At the time they were doing prototype work on the new F-Body platform... after seeing just how much detail work is done- and structural testing- I certainly wouldn't recommend trying to adapt another roof to the fiero- find a junker and use it!  I'm pretty sure that finding another roof would be really diffucult due to the frameless fiero window- its quite unique.  Check ebay regularly... they do show up- also I saw a website from a guy in illinois who may have something available (sorry, no address)!  Good Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||07-21-2001||02:47 PM||||F-body T-tops are huge. I doubt that they would fit on a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DecadenceR||07-21-2001||03:22 PM||||Theonly thing that I think would fit size-wise are a 1st gen MR2, maybe a Nissan Pulsar. But i agree with everyone else, just find one in a yard and do the swap. Don't forget to re-inforce the frame though||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||07-21-2001||03:40 PM||||I had a wreaked t-top fiero and couldnt give the parts away awhile back||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||07-21-2001||04:27 PM||||factory and contracted t top fieros have more structure reinforcement than regular fieros? what do they use and how is it done?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||07-21-2001||05:35 PM||||There is no additional frame reinforcement with the original T-Top for the Fiero. The 'H' bar took the place of the space frame side rails that are removed to do the conversion.<P>Cadaver;<BR>How about those trim caps?<BR>Got any time now?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Toddster||07-21-2001||05:36 PM||||I've always thought that the T-tops from a mid-80s Mustang would work with the right persuasion. They are plentiful in the wrecking yards. <P>I've never measured them up but they seem to be very close in size after a quick look.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Indiana_resto_guy||07-21-2001||09:20 PM||||Toddster - - - - now that's a thought.||||reg||1
